{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc | sed -n '1,430p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker.authority\n     2\t  \"Section 8.2 of docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md: the fail-closed,\n     3\t   proof-carrying name-authority policy behind the linker's name\n     4\t   environment. `name-environment` is a pure function over plain data:\n     5\t   it folds an authority map and a sequence of authority events\n     6\t   (assertion and retraction envelopes with their proofs) into a\n     7\t   name-environment snapshot plus diagnostics, and touches no stream,\n     8\t   no format record, no fetch path, and no kernel. The only\n     9\t   dependencies are the committed `dao.jing` content identities\n    10\t   (`segment-key`, `canonical-bytes`) and the composition-supplied\n    11\t   verify function the authority map carries: no cryptographic\n    12\t   primitive is implemented here.\n    13\t\n    14\t  Envelope shapes, the three per-principal passes, the retraction\n    15\t  binding, and the per-name fold are exactly the section 8.2 policy:\n    16\t  shape-validated envelopes by declared principals are honored only\n    17\t  with a valid proof; duplicates collapse by content id; equal\n    18\t  sequences from one principal are equivocation; sequences at or below\n    19\t  the floor are replays; a retraction removes exactly the assertion\n    20\t  its :yin.module/of names; and more than one remaining manifest\n    21\t  address for a name refuses :ambiguous-name with no tie-break rule.\"\n    22\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]))\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\t;; =============================================================================\n    26\t;; Envelopes and content ids (section 8.2)\n    27\t;; =============================================================================\n    28\t\n    29\t(defn assertion-id\n    30\t  \"The content address of an authority envelope: its `dao.jing`\n    31\t   segment-key. This is the id a retraction's :yin.module/of names.\"\n    32\t  [env]\n    33\t  (jing/segment-key env))\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(defn- envelope-defect\n    37\t  \"The first shape defect of env, or nil when env is a well-formed\n    38\t   assertion or retraction envelope. Manifest and retraction target\n    39\t   are checked by `dao.jing/segment-address?`, the authoritative\n    40\t   closed-registry address check.\"\n    41\t  [env]\n    42\t  (if (map? env)\n    43\t    (case (get env :yin.module/op)\n    44\t      :assert (cond\n    45\t                (not (symbol? (get env :yin.module/name))) :bad-name\n    46\t                (not (jing/segment-address?\n    47\t                       (get env :yin.module/manifest))) :bad-manifest\n    48\t                (nil? (get env :yin.module/asserted-by)) :bad-asserted-by\n    49\t                :else (if (int? (get env :yin.module/seq)) nil :bad-seq))\n    50\t      :retract (cond\n    51\t                 (not (jing/segment-address?\n    52\t                        (get env :yin.module/of))) :bad-of\n    53\t                 (nil? (get env :yin.module/asserted-by)) :bad-asserted-by\n    54\t                 :else (if (int? (get env :yin.module/seq)) nil :bad-seq))\n    55\t      :bad-op)\n    56\t    :not-an-envelope))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t;; =============================================================================\n    60\t;; Datom ingestion (section 8.2)\n    61\t;; =============================================================================\n    62\t\n    63\t(defn events-from-datoms\n    64\t  \"The section 8.2 authority event sequence, assembled from the\n    65\t   assertion datoms a composition read at its snapshot: every\n    66\t   `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]` datom yields one event whose proof is\n    67\t   the one `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]` value of the same entity. An\n    68\t   entity carrying two distinct proof values has no proof: none is\n    69\t   picked, so the event is the no-proof case, whatever the datom order.\n    70\t   An envelope datom with no proof datom is the no-proof case the policy\n    71\t   discards as :unauthenticated; a proof datom with no envelope datom\n    72\t   names no event and is ignored -- section 8.2's diagnostic kinds are a\n    73\t   closed set, and an orphan proof is no envelope at all. `carrier` is\n    74\t   the :dao.stream/identity of the one stream the composition read at\n    75\t   the snapshot, marked on every event for the attested check; nil means\n    76\t   the read names no stream, and an attested proof fails :bad-proof\n    77\t   there. Events keep the handed datoms' order, and the datoms are\n    78\t   already snapshot-bounded by the reader: nothing here reads or\n    79\t   advances a snapshot itself.\"\n    80\t  ([datoms] (events-from-datoms datoms nil))\n    81\t  ([datoms carrier]\n    82\t   (let [proof-of (reduce-kv\n    83\t                    (fn [acc e vs]\n    84\t                      (cond-> acc\n    85\t                        (= 1 (count vs)) (assoc e (first vs))))\n    86\t                    {}\n    87\t                    (reduce (fn [acc [e a v]]\n    88\t                              (cond-> acc\n    89\t                                (= a :yin.module/proof)\n    90\t                                (update e (fnil conj #{}) v)))\n    91\t                            {}\n    92\t                            datoms))]\n    93\t     (into []\n    94\t           (keep (fn [[e a v]]\n    95\t                   (when (= a :yin.module/envelope)\n    96\t                     (cond-> {:yin.module/envelope v}\n    97\t                       (contains? proof-of e)\n    98\t                       (assoc :yin.module/proof (get proof-of e))\n    99\t                       (some? carrier)\n   100\t                       (assoc :dao.stream/identity carrier)))))\n   101\t           datoms))))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t;; =============================================================================\n   105\t;; Authentication: the two proof kinds (section 8.2)\n   106\t;; =============================================================================\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn- proof-state\n   109\t  \"nil when the event's proof is valid for the principal's declaration,\n   110\t   else the authentication failure: :no-proof, :bad-proof, or\n   111\t   :no-proof-kind when the declaration admits neither proof kind and\n   112\t   the principal cannot assert anything. The verify function's answer\n   113\t   is taken as given; it is composition-supplied host code and is\n   114\t   expected not to throw.\"\n   115\t  [decl event]\n   116\t  (let [proof (get event :yin.module/proof)]\n   117\t    (case (get decl :proof)\n   118\t      :yin.module/signature\n   119\t      (if (map? proof)\n   120\t        (let [sig (get proof :yin.module/signature)]\n   121\t          (if (nil? sig)\n   122\t            :no-proof\n   123\t            (let [verify (get decl :verify)]\n   124\t              (when-not (and verify\n   125\t                             (verify (get decl :key)\n   126\t                                     (jing/canonical-bytes\n   127\t                                       (get event :yin.module/envelope))\n   128\t                                     sig))\n   129\t                :bad-proof))))\n   130\t        :no-proof)\n   131\t      :yin.module/attested\n   132\t      (if (map? proof)\n   133\t        (let [declared (get decl :dao.stream/identity)]\n   134\t          (if (nil? (get proof :yin.module/attested))\n   135\t            :no-proof\n   136\t            ;; the envelope must have been read from the declared log:\n   137\t            ;; copied onto another stream it carries no proof\n   138\t            (if (or (not= declared (get proof :yin.module/attested))\n   139\t                    (not= declared (get event :dao.stream/identity)))\n   140\t              :bad-proof\n   141\t              nil)))\n   142\t        :no-proof)\n   143\t      :no-proof-kind)))\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t(defn- discard-reason\n   147\t  \"The section 8.2 discard reason of an authentication failure kind.\"\n   148\t  [kind]\n   149\t  (case kind\n   150\t    :no-proof :unauthenticated\n   151\t    :bad-proof :unauthenticated\n   152\t    :no-proof-kind :undeclared-principal\n   153\t    kind))\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   156\t(defn- env-diagnostic\n   157\t  \"The diagnostic entry for one discarded envelope.\"\n   158\t  [kind reason env extra]\n   159\t  (merge {:kind kind\n   160\t          :reason reason\n   161\t          :id (when (some? env) (assertion-id env))\n   162\t          :op (when (map? env) (get env :yin.module/op))\n   163\t          :principal (when (map? env) (get env :yin.module/asserted-by))\n   164\t          :seq (when (map? env) (get env :yin.module/seq))}\n   165\t         extra))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t;; =============================================================================\n   169\t;; The three per-principal passes (section 8.2)\n   170\t;; =============================================================================\n   171\t\n   172\t(defn- honor-passes\n   173\t  \"The three passes over one principal's proven envelopes: deduplicate\n   174\t   by content id (duplicate appearances beyond the first drop\n   175\t   silently), detect equivocation on equal sequence (every envelope of\n   176\t   the principal from the first equivocating sequence on is discarded\n   177\t   as equivocation), then order by sequence and honor each envelope\n   178\t   only past the floor and every sequence honored before it. Returns\n   179\t   {:honored [...] :diagnostics [...]}.\"\n   180\t  [decl proven]\n   181\t  (let [deduped (::kept\n   182\t                  (reduce (fn [acc cand]\n   183\t                            (if (contains? (::seen acc) (:id cand))\n   184\t                              acc\n   185\t                              (-> acc\n   186\t                                  (update ::kept conj cand)\n   187\t                                  (update ::seen conj (:id cand)))))\n   188\t                          {::kept [] ::seen #{}}\n   189\t                          proven))\n   190\t        by-seq (group-by :seq deduped)\n   191\t        eq-min (when-let [eqs (seq (keep (fn [[s cands]]\n   192\t                                           (when (> (count cands) 1) s))\n   193\t                                         by-seq))]\n   194\t                 (reduce min eqs))\n   195\t        {kept :kept equated :equated}\n   196\t        (if eq-min\n   197\t          (group-by (fn [cand]\n   198\t                      (if (>= (:seq cand) eq-min)\n   199\t                        :equated :kept))\n   200\t                    deduped)\n   201\t          {:kept deduped})\n   202\t        floor (or (get decl :seq-floor) 0)\n   203\t        done (reduce (fn [acc cand]\n   204\t                       (if (> (:seq cand) (::last-honored acc))\n   205\t                         (-> acc\n   206\t                             (assoc ::last-honored (:seq cand))\n   207\t                             (update ::honored conj cand))\n   208\t                         (update acc ::replayed conj cand)))\n   209\t                     {::last-honored floor ::honored [] ::replayed []}\n   210\t                     (sort-by :seq (or kept [])))]\n   211\t    {:honored (::honored done)\n   212\t     :diagnostics\n   213\t     (into (mapv (fn [cand]\n   214\t                   (env-diagnostic :equivocation :equivocation\n   215\t                                   (:env cand) nil))\n   216\t                 (or equated []))\n   217\t           (mapv (fn [cand]\n   218\t                   (env-diagnostic :replay :replay (:env cand) nil))\n   219\t                 (::replayed done)))}))\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t;; =============================================================================\n   223\t;; The per-name fold (section 8.2)\n   224\t;; =============================================================================\n   225\t\n   226\t(defn- name-entry\n   227\t  \"The outcome for one name: :absent for zero remaining assertions, a\n   228\t   successful resolution with provenance for exactly one distinct\n   229\t   manifest address, :ambiguous-name naming every remaining address\n   230\t   and asserter for more than one. Entries are ordered by address, so\n   231\t   the outcome never depends on carrier order, recency, or sequence.\"\n   232\t  [decls snapshot cands]\n   233\t  (let [entries (sort-by (fn [e] (str (:address e) \" \" (:asserter e)))\n   234\t                         (distinct\n   235\t                           (map (fn [cand]\n   236\t                                  {:address (get (:env cand)\n   237\t                                                 :yin.module/manifest)\n   238\t                                   :asserter (:principal cand)})\n   239\t                                cands)))\n   240\t        addresses (distinct (map :address entries))\n   241\t        asserters (distinct (map :asserter entries))]\n   242\t    (case (count addresses)\n   243\t      0 {:status :refused :reason :absent}\n   244\t      1 {:status :ok\n   245\t         :address (first addresses)\n   246\t         :yin.link/provenance\n   247\t         {:yin.module/asserted-by (vec asserters)\n   248\t          :yin.link/proof-kind\n   249\t          (vec (distinct (map (fn [p] (get (get decls p) :proof))\n   250\t                              asserters)))\n   251\t          :yin.link/snapshot snapshot}}\n   252\t      {:status :refused\n   253\t       :reason :ambiguous-name\n   254\t       :addresses (vec addresses)\n   255\t       :asserters (vec asserters)})))\n   256\t\n   257\t\n   258\t(defn name-environment\n   259\t  \"Fold `events` under `authority` into the name-environment snapshot\n   260\t   of section 8.2.\n   261\t\n   262\t   `authority` is a map with the snapshot under :snapshot (an index\n   263\t   manifest address or a stream cursor; it is echoed and never\n   264\t   dereferenced here) and the accepted principals under :principals.\n   265\t   A signature principal declares {:proof :yin.module/signature\n   266\t   :key k :verify f}; f is composition-supplied and is called as\n   267\t   (f key canonical-bytes sig). An attested principal declares\n   268\t   {:proof :yin.module/attested :dao.stream/identity id} and every\n   269\t   envelope must have been read from that stream. Either may carry\n   270\t   :seq-floor, the highest sequence already honored for a re-declared\n   271\t   principal (0 for a new one).\n   272\t\n   273\t   Each event is a map: :yin.module/envelope, :yin.module/proof, and,\n   274\t   for the attested check, the :dao.stream/identity the envelope was\n   275\t   read from. An envelope whose proof is absent or fails is\n   276\t   :unauthenticated and is discarded before counting.\n   277\t\n   278\t   Returns {:names {name entry} :diagnostics [...] :honored-seq\n   279\t   {principal highest-honored-sequence} :snapshot s}. Advancing the\n   280\t   snapshot is a fresh call with the advanced authority and events\n   281\t   (the next floor is :honored-seq), never an ambient re-read.\"\n   282\t  [authority events]\n   283\t  (let [decls (:principals authority)\n   284\t        {stage1 :diagnostics proven :proven name-set :names}\n   285\t        (reduce\n   286\t          (fn [acc event]\n   287\t            (let [env (when (map? event)\n   288\t                        (get event :yin.module/envelope))]\n   289\t              (if-some [defect (envelope-defect env)]\n   290\t                (update acc :diagnostics conj\n   291\t                        (env-diagnostic :malformed-envelope\n   292\t                                        :malformed-envelope\n   293\t                                        env {:defect defect}))\n   294\t                (let [principal (get env :yin.module/asserted-by)\n   295\t                      acc (if (= :assert (get env :yin.module/op))\n   296\t                            (update acc :names conj\n   297\t                                    (get env :yin.module/name))\n   298\t                            acc)]\n   299\t                  (if-not (contains? decls principal)\n   300\t                    (update acc :diagnostics conj\n   301\t                            (env-diagnostic :undeclared-principal\n   302\t                                            :undeclared-principal\n   303\t                                            env nil))\n   304\t                    (if-some [failed (proof-state (get decls principal)\n   305\t                                                  event)]\n   306\t                      (update acc :diagnostics conj\n   307\t                              (env-diagnostic failed\n   308\t                                              (discard-reason failed)\n   309\t                                              env nil))\n   310\t                      (update acc :proven conj\n   311\t                              {:env env\n   312\t                               :id (assertion-id env)\n   313\t                               :principal principal\n   314\t                               :seq (get env :yin.module/seq)})))))))\n   315\t          {:diagnostics [] :proven [] :names #{}}\n   316\t          events)\n   317\t        per-principal\n   318\t        (mapv (fn [principal]\n   319\t                (let [mine (filter (fn [cand]\n   320\t                                     (= principal (:principal cand)))\n   321\t                                   proven)\n   322\t                      {:keys [honored diagnostics]}\n   323\t                      (honor-passes (get decls principal) mine)]\n   324\t                  {:principal principal\n   325\t                   :honored honored\n   326\t                   :diagnostics diagnostics}))\n   327\t              (distinct (mapv :principal proven)))\n   328\t        honored (mapcat :honored per-principal)\n   329\t        {assertions true retractions false}\n   330\t        (group-by (fn [cand]\n   331\t                    (= :assert (get (:env cand) :yin.module/op)))\n   332\t                  honored)\n   333\t        by-principal (group-by :principal assertions)\n   334\t        {retracted true dangling false}\n   335\t        (group-by (fn [cand]\n   336\t                    (contains?\n   337\t                      (set (map :id (get by-principal\n   338\t                                         (:principal cand))))\n   339\t                      (get (:env cand) :yin.module/of)))\n   340\t                  (or retractions []))\n   341\t        retracted-ids (set (map (fn [cand]\n   342\t                                  (get (:env cand) :yin.module/of))\n   343\t                                (or retracted [])))\n   344\t        surviving (remove (fn [cand]\n   345\t                            (contains? retracted-ids (:id cand)))\n   346\t                          (or assertions []))\n   347\t        by-name (group-by (fn [cand]\n   348\t                            (get (:env cand) :yin.module/name))\n   349\t                          surviving)]\n   350\t    {:names (into {}\n   351\t                  (map (fn [nm]\n   352\t                         [nm (name-entry decls (:snapshot authority)\n   353\t                                         (get by-name nm))]))\n   354\t                  name-set)\n   355\t     :diagnostics (vec (concat stage1\n   356\t                               (mapcat :diagnostics per-principal)\n   357\t                               (map (fn [cand]\n   358\t                                      (env-diagnostic\n   359\t                                        :dangling-retraction\n   360\t                                        :dangling-retraction\n   361\t                                        (:env cand)\n   362\t                                        {:of (get (:env cand)\n   363\t                                                  :yin.module/of)}))\n   364\t                                    (or dangling []))))\n   365\t     :honored-seq (into {}\n   366\t                        (keep (fn [pr]\n   367\t                                (when (seq (:honored pr))\n   368\t                                  [(:principal pr)\n   369\t                                   (reduce max (map :seq (:honored pr)))])))\n   370\t                        per-principal)\n   371\t     :snapshot (:snapshot authority)}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1680,1775p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker_authority_ingestion_test.cljc | sed -n '260,365p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1680,1775p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker_authority_ingestion_test.cljc | sed -n '260,365p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1680\t- The manifest is verified like any content: a `:yin.module/manifest`\n  1681\t  format record with `:identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?`, a\n  1682\t  validator over the keys above, no parts, no obligations.\n  1683\t\n  1684\t### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\n  1685\t\n  1686\tNames live outside the manifest. A name environment maps a module name\n  1687\tto a manifest address and is linker-local state in one of two shapes:\n  1688\t\n  1689\t- a plain map `{'my.lib :segment/...}`, for tests and single-process\n  1690\t  compositions, with the composition itself as the sole asserter;\n  1691\t- assertions read from a `dao.space` source under the policy below.\n  1692\t\n  1693\t**Fail-closed assertion policy.** This policy is an entry criterion for\n  1694\tM4: no linker may resolve a name from `dao.space` assertions before it is\n  1695\timplemented and tested. The policy lives in `yin.vm.linker.authority`,\n  1696\tas a pure function over plain data.\n  1697\t\n  1698\t- **Every authority event is a signed envelope.** An assertion and a\n  1699\t  retraction are two distinct envelope shapes, each a plain map whose\n  1700\t  content address (`dao.jing/segment-key`) is the event's id:\n  1701\t\n  1702\t  ```clojure\n  1703\t  ;; assertion\n  1704\t  {:yin.module/op          :assert\n  1705\t   :yin.module/name        'my.lib\n  1706\t   :yin.module/manifest    :segment/...\n  1707\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\n  1708\t   :yin.module/seq         41}          ; per-principal, strictly rising\n  1709\t\n  1710\t  ;; retraction: bound to one assertion by that assertion's id\n  1711\t  {:yin.module/op          :retract\n  1712\t   :yin.module/of          :segment/... ; segment-key of the assertion\n  1713\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\n  1714\t   :yin.module/seq         42}\n  1715\t  ```\n  1716\t\n  1717\t  The envelope is transacted as datoms `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]`\n  1718\t  and `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]`. Ingestion is\n  1719\t  `yin.vm.linker.authority/events-from-datoms`: one event per envelope\n  1720\t  datom, carrying its entity's proof value (an envelope with no\n  1721\t  proof datom, or whose entity carries two distinct proof values, is the\n  1722\t  no-proof case below; a proof datom with no envelope datom names no\n  1723\t  event, and joins one only if an envelope later appears on its entity), with the carrier\n  1724\t  `:dao.stream/identity` of the read supplied by the composition, never\n  1725\t  read from a datom. An envelope is honored only with\n  1726\t  a proof; a bare `:asserted-by` value is a string anyone can write.\n  1727\t  An envelope whose proof is absent or fails is `:unauthenticated`\n  1728\t  with `:kind :no-proof` or `:bad-proof` and is discarded before\n  1729\t  counting. A retraction whose `:yin.module/of` names no assertion at\n  1730\t  the snapshot, or an assertion by a different principal, is discarded\n  1731\t  with `:kind :dangling-retraction`; a retraction retracts exactly the\n  1732\t  assertion it names and nothing by name alone.\n  1733\t- **Replay is prevented by the per-principal sequence.** Every envelope\n  1734\t  a principal issues carries `:yin.module/seq`, strictly increasing\n  1735\t  over that principal's lifetime; the composition declares each\n  1736\t  principal's floor in `:authority` (`0` for a new principal, the\n  1737\t  highest sequence already honored for a re-declared one). The\n  1738\t  declaration carries that floor as `:seq-floor`. At the snapshot the\n  1739\t  linker processes one principal's proven envelopes in three passes,\n  1740\t  in this order:\n  1741\t  1. *Deduplicate by content id.* Every envelope is content; two\n  1742\t     appearances of one envelope have one `segment-key` and are one\n  1743\t     event. All but the first appearance are dropped silently, as\n  1744\t     `dao.jing` drops a re-materialization: an exact duplicate is a\n  1745\t     harmless carrier replay (a forwarder, a retry after `full`, a\n  1746\t     mirrored log) and is neither a defect nor evidence against the\n  1747\t     principal. This pass runs first so that repeating a valid envelope\n  1748\t     can never suppress it.\n  1749\t  2. *Detect equivocation.* After deduplication, two *distinct*\n  1750\t     envelopes from one principal with equal sequence are equivocation:\n  1751\t     the principal signed two different claims under one sequence\n  1752\t     number. Both are discarded with `:kind :equivocation`, and the\n  1753\t     principal's later envelopes at the snapshot are discarded too. A\n  1754\t     duplicate can no longer reach this pass, so equivocation is\n  1755\t     attributable to the signer alone. The pair and every later\n  1756\t     envelope of that principal are discarded with\n  1757\t     `:kind :equivocation`.\n  1758\t  3. *Order and honor.* The remaining envelopes are ordered by sequence\n  1759\t     and each is honored only if its sequence exceeds the floor and\n  1760\t     every sequence honored before it; an envelope at or below either\n  1761\t     is a replay of an old claim under a fresh carrier and is discarded\n  1762\t     with `:kind :replay`.\n  1763\t  A monotone sequence is chosen over nonces because it makes the check\n  1764\t  stateless over the snapshot: no nonce store is needed and no window\n  1765\t  is guessed.\n  1766\t  A wall-clock timestamp is admitted as an optional\n  1767\t  `:yin.module/issued-at` in the envelope for audit, and is never used\n  1768\t  to order or to accept.\n  1769\t- Two proof kinds are admitted, and the composition's `:authority`\n  1770\t  declares, per principal, which one it expects:\n  1771\t  - *Signature.* `proof` is `{:yin.module/signature sig}`, where `sig`\n  1772\t    signs the canonical bytes (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) of the whole\n  1773\t    envelope under the principal's public key, so operation type, name,\n  1774\t    manifest, principal, and sequence are all covered and none can be\n  1775\t    altered or recombined. `:authority` holds, per principal, the key\n   260\t;; =============================================================================\n   261\t\n   262\t(deftest attested-datoms-prove-only-through-the-reads-carrier\n   263\t  (let [log (open-space)\n   264\t        a (addr [:m 1])\n   265\t        env (assertion-env 'reporter 'log.lib a 1)\n   266\t        t (:dao.space/t\n   267\t            (commit! log\n   268\t                     [[:db/add \"tid_ev\" :yin.module/envelope env]\n   269\t                      [:db/add \"tid_ev\" :yin.module/proof\n   270\t                       {:yin.module/attested :dao.stream/log-1}]]))\n   271\t        decls {'reporter (attested-decl :dao.stream/log-1)}]\n   272\t    (testing \"read from the declared stream, the envelope is proven\"\n   273\t      (let [snap (authority/name-environment\n   274\t                   {:snapshot t :principals decls}\n   275\t                   (events-at log t :dao.stream/log-1))]\n   276\t        (is (= :ok (:status (entry snap 'log.lib))))\n   277\t        (is (= a (:address (entry snap 'log.lib))))\n   278\t        (is (empty? (:diagnostics snap)))))\n   279\t    (testing \"the same datoms read from nowhere carry no proof\"\n   280\t      (let [snap (authority/name-environment\n   281\t                   {:snapshot t :principals decls}\n   282\t                   (events-at log t))]\n   283\t        (is (= :absent (:reason (entry snap 'log.lib))))\n   284\t        (is (= 1 (count (discards snap :bad-proof))))))))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t;; =============================================================================\n   288\t;; One proof per event entity, whatever the datom order\n   289\t;; =============================================================================\n   290\t\n   291\t(deftest two-distinct-proofs-on-one-entity-fail-closed\n   292\t  (let [log (open-space)\n   293\t        env (assertion-env 'alice 'my.lib (addr [:m 1]) 1)\n   294\t        t (:dao.space/t\n   295\t            (commit! log\n   296\t                     [[:db/add \"tid_ev\" :yin.module/envelope env]\n   297\t                      [:db/add \"tid_ev\" :yin.module/proof\n   298\t                       {:yin.module/signature (fake-sign env)}]\n   299\t                      [:db/add \"tid_ev\" :yin.module/proof\n   300\t                       {:yin.module/signature \"forged\"}]]))\n   301\t        events (events-at log t)\n   302\t        snap (authority/name-environment\n   303\t               {:snapshot t :principals {'alice (sig-decl 'alice)}}\n   304\t               events)]\n   305\t    (is (= 1 (count events)))\n   306\t    (is (not (contains? (first events) :yin.module/proof)))\n   307\t    (is (= :absent (:reason (entry snap 'my.lib))))\n   308\t    (is (= 1 (count (discards snap :no-proof))))))\n   309\t\n   310\t\n   311\t(deftest ingestion-is-invariant-under-datom-permutation\n   312\t  (let [env (assertion-env 'alice 'my.lib (addr [:m 1]) 1)\n   313\t        good {:yin.module/signature (fake-sign env)}\n   314\t        bad {:yin.module/signature \"forged\"}\n   315\t        datoms [[1 :yin.module/envelope env]\n   316\t                [1 :yin.module/proof good]\n   317\t                [1 :yin.module/proof bad]\n   318\t                [2 :yin.module/envelope env]\n   319\t                [2 :yin.module/proof good]]\n   320\t        result (fn [ds] (frequencies (authority/events-from-datoms ds)))\n   321\t        expected (result datoms)]\n   322\t    (doseq [ds [(reverse datoms)\n   323\t                (concat (drop 2 datoms) (take 2 datoms))\n   324\t                [(nth datoms 2) (nth datoms 4) (nth datoms 0)\n   325\t                 (nth datoms 3) (nth datoms 1)]]]\n   326\t      (is (= expected (result ds))))))\n   327\t\n   328\t\n   329\t(deftest orphan-proof-joins-a-later-envelope-deterministically\n   330\t  (let [env (assertion-env 'alice 'my.lib (addr [:m 1]) 1)\n   331\t        proof {:yin.module/signature (fake-sign env)}\n   332\t        orphan [[7 :yin.module/proof proof]]\n   333\t        joined [[7 :yin.module/proof proof]\n   334\t                [7 :yin.module/envelope env]]]\n   335\t    (is (empty? (authority/events-from-datoms orphan)))\n   336\t    (is (= [{:yin.module/envelope env :yin.module/proof proof}]\n   337\t           (authority/events-from-datoms joined)\n   338\t           (authority/events-from-datoms (reverse joined))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
