{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1790430690002-architect-linker-m4-a3-gate.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log'","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a0dd69-cb8b-7830-8555-bf8bbf48c089\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’ll check the uncommitted diff against the linker and UCF specs, then trace the ingestion code and tests. I’ll use the orchestrator’s test results and won’t rerun suites or edit files.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/code-review-pr/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/code-review-pr/SKILL.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"---\\nname: code-review-pr\\ndescription: >-\\n  Performs comprehensive, high-quality code reviews on Git pull requests, branches, commit ranges, or local working tree diffs. Analyzes code correctness, security, architecture, test coverage, and performance using automated diff analysis and structured review checklists.\\n---\\n\\n# Code Review PR Skill\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nThe `code-review-pr` skill provides an end-to-end framework for conducting rigorous, actionable code reviews on Git pull requests, feature branches, commit ranges, or working tree diffs. It combines automated diff scanning via `scripts/pr_reviewer.py` with structured review checklists across security, correctness, architecture, performance, and testing.\\n\\nUse this skill whenever asked to:\\n- Review a pull request or feature branch (`git diff main...HEAD`).\\n- Review recent commits (`git diff HEAD~1` or commit range).\\n- Review uncommitted local changes (`git diff` or staged changes).\\n- Perform a security, quality, or architecture audit of proposed code changes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\nRun the automated PR reviewer script to generate an initial risk assessment, churn metrics, and automated smell scan:\\n\\n```bash\\n# 1. Review branch changes against main (Default PR review)\\npython3 .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze --target main...HEAD\\n\\n# 2. Review last commit\\npython3 .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze --target HEAD~1\\n\\n# 3. Review uncommitted working tree changes\\npython3 .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze --target working\\n\\n# 4. Save review report to file\\npython3 .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze --target main...HEAD --output review_report.md\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Code Review Workflow\\n\\nFollow this step-by-step process when executing a code review:\\n\\n### Step 1: Run Automated Diff Analysis\\nExecute `scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze` for the target Git ref/range. Review the output to determine:\\n- Total lines added/deleted and file churn distribution.\\n- High-risk modified files (e.g., Security/Auth, Database/Schema, Infrastructure, API Contracts).\\n- Test-to-source additions ratio.\\n- Automated static findings (hardcoded secrets, debug leftovers, swallowed exceptions, SQL injection risks).\\n\\n### Step 2: Deep-Dive Code Inspection\\nInspect the diffs for high-risk files using `git diff <target> -- <path>` or `view_file`. Focus on:\\n1. **Logic & Edge Cases**:\\n   - Boundary checks, null/nil handling, empty collections, zero division.\\n   - Resource leaks (unclosed streams, file handles, DB connections).\\n   - Race conditions, shared state mutation, concurrency locks.\\n2. **Security & Credentials**:\\n   - No hardcoded API keys, passwords, or tokens.\\n   - Input validation before execution or query interpolation.\\n   - Proper authorization checks on new or updated endpoints.\\n3. **Architecture & Contracts**:\\n   - Preserving backward compatibility on existing API functions/endpoints.\\n   - Proper module separation and clean interface boundaries.\\n4. **Test Coverage & Quality**:\\n   - Ensuring new source logic is accompanied by unit/integration tests.\\n   - Verifying tests validate actual assertions rather than just non-crashing execution.\\n\\n### Step 3: Reference Checklist & Severity Taxonomy\\nConsult [references/review_checklist.md](references/review_checklist.md) to classify findings:\\n- **P0 (Critical / Blocker)**: Security breaches, data loss risks, severe crashes, hardcoded credentials.\\n- **P1 (High / Must Address)**: Logic bugs, broken API contracts, swallowed exceptions, missing critical tests.\\n- **P2 (Medium / Recommended)**: Performance bottlenecks, code duplication, missing parameter validation.\\n- **P3 (Low / Suggestion)**: Minor formatting, naming improvements, leftover comments/TODOs.\\n\\n### Step 4: Formulate Structured Review Report\\nPresent findings to the user using the following template:\\n\\n```markdown\\n# 🔍 Code Review Report\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n- **Target:** `<git-ref>`\\n- **Verdict:** `[ APPROVED | REQUEST CHANGES | COMMENT ]`\\n- **Overall Risk:** `[ LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH ]`\\n- **Metrics:** `X files changed, +Y / -Z lines`\\n\\n## 🚨 Critical Findings (P0 / P1)\\n- **[Severity]** `path/to/file.ext:L123` - Short issue description.\\n  ```diff\\n  - problematic code\\n  + suggested fix\\n  ```\\n\\n## 💡 Improvements & Suggestions (P2 / P3)\\n- **[Severity]** `path/to/file.ext` - Recommendation details.\\n\\n## 🧪 Test Coverage & Quality Assessment\\n- Evaluation of test ratio and edge case coverage.\\n\\n## 🌟 Positive Highlights\\n- Clean implementations, thorough documentation, or well-structured refactoring.\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Utility Script Reference\\n\\nThe bundled helper script `scripts/pr_reviewer.py` supports the following options:\\n\\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `--target` | String | `main...HEAD` | Git range/ref (`main...HEAD`, `HEAD~1`, `staged`, `working`) |\\n| `--output` | String | None | File path to write report output |\\n| `--format` | String | `markdown` | Output format (`markdown` or `json`) |\\n| `--repo-dir` | String | Current Dir | Path to the target Git repository |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Common Review Pitfalls\\n\\n1. **Nit Tunnel Vision**: Focusing heavily on formatting or naming while missing underlying logic bugs or edge-case crashes.\\n2. **Ignoring Test Ratio**: Approving large source code changes without verifying corresponding test coverage additions.\\n3. **Swallowing Symptoms**: Suggesting `try/except` wrappers around failing code rather than addressing root cause invalid inputs or broken state.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790417540104-vm-engineer-linker-m4-a3-authority-ingestion.glm-5.3.report.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790417540104-vm-engineer-linker-m4-a3-authority-ingestion.glm-5.3.report.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-09-26 10:12:20 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-09-26 17:12:20 +0700\\nCoding-Agent: glm\\nSession-ID: 5985a4e0-f658-4d44-b6c9-2d2f318994b8\\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-09-26 10:24:14 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-26 17:24:14 +07\\n\\n# yin.vm.linker M4 slice A3: authority-policy datom ingestion\\n\\nRole: VM Runtime Engineer. Branch m4-a3\\n(worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-a3,\\nbase 9428c3d2 = master). Nothing committed, staged, or merged, per the rules.\\n\\n## What was built\\n\\n`yin.vm.linker.authority/events-from-datoms`\\n(src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc,\\nnew function between the envelope/content-id section and the authentication\\nsection): the section 8.2 authority event sequence assembled from the assertion\\ndatoms a composition read at its snapshot, following linker.cljc's\\n`index-from-datoms` pattern. Two arities:\\n\\n- `(events-from-datoms datoms)` and `(events-from-datoms datoms carrier)`.\\n- Every `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]` datom yields exactly one event\\n  `{:yin.module/envelope env ...}` whose proof is the FIRST\\n  `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]` datom of the same entity (first in handed\\n  order; the dao.space current view hands EAVT-ordered facts, so this is\\n  deterministic).\\n- `carrier`, when given, marks every event with that `:dao.stream/identity`\\n  (the one stream the composition read at the snapshot) for the attested-log\\n  check; nil means the read names no stream, and an attested proof fails\\n  :bad-proof there (fail closed).\\n- Pure over the handed datoms: no ambient read, no snapshot advance, no atoms,\\n  no clock, no reader conditionals; events keep the handed datoms' order.\\n  name-environment and every A1/A2 deftest are untouched (verified: the A1/A2\\n  test file is not in the diff; the namespace still passes).\\n\\n## Decisions the spec left open (and why)\\n\\n1. **Orphan proof datom: IGNORED, not reported.** The task allowed either.\\n   Section 8.2's diagnostics are a closed set -- the four discard kinds plus\\n   exactly `:malformed-envelope`, `:undeclared-principal`, `:no-proof-kind`\\n   (L1806-1810) -- and no kind describes a proof with no envelope; the policy's\\n   event shape is envelope-keyed, so an orphan proof names no event at all. The\\n   malformed-datoms test pins this: three datoms committed (envelope-no-proof,\\n   orphan proof, envelope-not-a-map), exactly two events assembled, and the\\n   diagnostic set is exactly #{:no-proof :malformed-envelope}.\\n2. **The attested carrier is a per-read argument, not a datom.** Section 8.2\\n   names only two datom shapes; \\\"every envelope read from that identity\\\"\\n   (L1777-1780) makes the carrier a property of the read (which stream the\\n   composition read at the cursor), like the snapshot itself. Recorded in the\\n   one added spec sentence and tested both ways.\\n3. **Multiple envelope datoms on one entity: one event per datom** (1:1 with\\n   the datoms, like index-from-datoms per-index-datom). A second envelope\\n   sharing one proof cannot both verify (the signature covers the whole\\n   envelope), so this stays fail closed with no arbitrary winner chosen.\\n   Not separately tested (degenerate datom shape; the no-proof/not-an-envelope\\n   paths cover the malformed datoms the task asked for).\\n\\n## Spec edit\\n\\nOne sentence added to section 8.2 (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md, after the\\n`[ev :yin.module/proof proof]` datom sentence, L1719-1724) recording decisions\\n1 and 2. No other section touched.\\n\\n## Files changed\\n\\n- src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc -- +39 lines, one new function\\n  (`events-from-datoms`), nothing else moved or edited.\\n- test/yin/vm/linker_authority_ingestion_test.cljc -- NEW, 5 deftests / 29\\n  assertions, end to end from transacted datoms (see below).\\n- docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md -- the one sentence above.\\n\\n## Tests added (all red first: the var did not exist, then green)\\n\\nEnd to end: commit real tx-data into an in-memory dao.space (dao.space\\ntransactor over a memory-log local stream, the ledger-test composition), read\\nat the snapshot through the query API (`current` view as-of bounded at the\\ncommitted cursor position, facts drained through `match`), ingest, fold with\\nname-environment:\\n\\n1. `transacted-assertion-datoms-resolve-the-name` -- the exact name environment\\n   asserted (full `:names` map equality, provenance with `:yin.link/snapshot`\\n   = the cursor position, empty diagnostics, `:honored-seq`).\\n2. `datom-transacted-after-the-snapshot-is-invisible-until-rebuilt` -- snapshot\\n   advance: the reads happen after BOTH commits, so the as-of bound alone\\n   decides; at t1 the later name does not exist (not even a diagnostic), the\\n   first snapshot is a value the second build never mutates, and the rebuilt\\n   snapshot at t2 resolves the new name.\\n3. `transacted-retraction-removes-exactly-its-assertion` -- a retraction\\n   envelope transacted as datoms removes exactly its named assertion; a\\n   same-named sibling and another name survive; no dangling retraction.\\n4. `malformed-authority-datoms-fail-closed` -- envelope with no proof datom\\n   (exactly one :no-proof, :unauthenticated), orphan proof datom (ignored, no\\n   event, no diagnostic), envelope datom whose value is not a map (exactly one\\n   :malformed-envelope, defect :not-an-envelope).\\n5. `attested-datoms-prove-only-through-the-reads-carrier` -- the same committed\\n   datoms resolve when read with the declared stream as carrier and fail\\n   :bad-proof when read from nowhere.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- TDD: red confirmed first (compile error, no such var events-from-datoms),\\n  then green.\\n- JVM lane `mise exec -- clojure -M:test`:\\n  - before (recorded first, this worktree at 9428c3d2): 2,138 tests /\\n    181,890 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. (The task brief said 181,898 at\\n    master; my measured baseline on this tree is 181,890 -- reported as\\n    measured.)\\n  - after: 2,143 tests / 181,920 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors\\n    (+5 tests, +30 assertions, exactly the new ingestion deftests; the\\n    selective run of the one namespace reports 29 assertions, the full\\n    suite 30 -- both from real logs, reported as measured).\\n- kondo: 0 errors, 0 warnings on both changed source files.\\n- cljstyle: clean on both changed source files.\\n- Every added/edited line is ASCII and <= 80 columns (checked mechanically).\\n- Cross-host safety: no reader conditionals added anywhere; no cross-namespace\\n  #'private access (test uses only public vars); only corpus-idiomatic core\\n  (reduce/assoc/contains?/into/keep/cond->/some?), all already used in the\\n  cljc corpus that compiles on JVM, Node, and Dart; the test's dao.space\\n  composition (transactor + memory-log + ringbuffer + query current/match) is\\n  the same one ledger_test.cljc already runs on all three hosts.\\n\\n## Unrun checks\\n\\n- Node and Dart lanes (the task assigns those to the orchestrator).\\n- No A1/A2 or name-environment behavior changed, so their cross-host results\\n  carry over unchanged except for the new shared-file compile (kondo and JVM\\n  clean; cljd has no new constructs).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git -C /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-a3 diff HEAD -- src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc test/yin/vm/linker_authority_ingestion_test.cljc docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git -C /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-m4-a3 diff HEAD -- src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc test/yin/vm/linker_authority_ingestion_test.cljc docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"2026-09-26 18:11:50.532 xcodebuild[61383:26313536]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\n2026-09-26 18:11:50.962 xcodebuild[61383:26313534] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\"Input/output error\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-oi8j8uFF' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n2026-09-26 18:11:51.708 xcodebuild[61392:26313631]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\n2026-09-26 18:11:51.917 xcodebuild[61392:26313626] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\"Input/output error\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\ndiff --git a/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md b/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md\\nindex 4a31f1af..fa63ab7f 100644\\n--- a/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md\\n+++ b/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md\\n@@ -1715,7 +1715,13 @@ as a pure function over plain data.\\n   ```\\n \\n   The envelope is transacted as datoms `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]`\\n-  and `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]`. An envelope is honored only with\\n+  and `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]`. Ingestion is\\n+  `yin.vm.linker.authority/events-from-datoms`: one event per envelope\\n+  datom, carrying its entity's first proof datom (an envelope with no\\n+  proof datom is the no-proof case below; a proof datom with no envelope\\n+  datom names no event and is ignored), with the carrier\\n+  `:dao.stream/identity` of the read supplied by the composition, never\\n+  read from a datom. An envelope is honored only with\\n   a proof; a bare `:asserted-by` value is a string anyone can write.\\n   An envelope whose proof is absent or fails is `:unauthenticated`\\n   with `:kind :no-proof` or `:bad-proof` and is discarded before\\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc\\nindex 8b877cf6..000ef1c6 100644\\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc\\n@@ -56,6 +56,45 @@\\n     :not-an-envelope))\\n \\n \\n+;; =============================================================================\\n+;; Datom ingestion (section 8.2)\\n+;; =============================================================================\\n+\\n+(defn events-from-datoms\\n+  \\\"The section 8.2 authority event sequence, assembled from the\\n+   assertion datoms a composition read at its snapshot: every\\n+   `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]` datom yields one event whose proof is\\n+   the first `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]` datom of the same entity.\\n+   An envelope datom with no proof datom is the no-proof case the policy\\n+   discards as :unauthenticated; a proof datom with no envelope datom\\n+   names no event and is ignored -- section 8.2's diagnostic kinds are a\\n+   closed set, and an orphan proof is no envelope at all. `carrier` is\\n+   the :dao.stream/identity of the one stream the composition read at\\n+   the snapshot, marked on every event for the attested check; nil means\\n+   the read names no stream, and an attested proof fails :bad-proof\\n+   there. Events keep the handed datoms' order, and the datoms are\\n+   already snapshot-bounded by the reader: nothing here reads or\\n+   advances a snapshot itself.\\\"\\n+  ([datoms] (events-from-datoms datoms nil))\\n+  ([datoms carrier]\\n+   (let [proof-of (reduce (fn [acc [e a v]]\\n+                            (if (and (= a :yin.module/proof)\\n+                                     (not (contains? acc e)))\\n+                              (assoc acc e v)\\n+                              acc))\\n+                          {}\\n+                          datoms)]\\n+     (into []\\n+           (keep (fn [[e a v]]\\n+                   (when (= a :yin.module/envelope)\\n+                     (cond-> {:yin.module/envelope v}\\n+                       (contains? proof-of e)\\n+                       (assoc :yin.module/proof (get proof-of e))\\n+                       (some? carrier)\\n+                       (assoc :dao.stream/identity carrier)))))\\n+           datoms))))\\n+\\n+\\n ;; =============================================================================\\n ;; Authentication: the two proof kinds (section 8.2)\\n ;; =============================================================================\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The tracked diff adds one ingestion function and a spec sentence; the new test file is untracked, so I’m reading it separately. I’ll check the first-proof and orphan-proof choices against the policy passes and the datastore’s ordering guarantees.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker_authority_ingestion_test.cljc | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker_authority_ingestion_test.cljc | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t(ns yin.vm.linker-authority-ingestion-test\\n     2\\t  \\\"Slice A3 (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md section 8.2): datom\\n     3\\t   ingestion. The section 8.2 assertion datoms -- `[ev\\n     4\\t   :yin.module/envelope env]` beside `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]` --\\n     5\\t   are committed to an in-memory dao.space, read at a snapshot through\\n     6\\t   the query API (the `current` view, as-of bounded at the committed\\n     7\\t   cursor position, its facts drained through `match`), and assembled by\\n     8\\t   `yin.vm.linker.authority/events-from-datoms` into exactly the event\\n     9\\t   sequence `name-environment` folds. Ingestion is pure over the datoms\\n    10\\t   it is handed: the source and the snapshot are the composition's, and\\n    11\\t   the tests below are the whole composition.\\\"\\n    12\\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n    13\\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\\n    14\\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\\n    15\\t            [dao.space.query :as query]\\n    16\\t            [dao.space.transact :as transact]\\n    17\\t            [dao.space.transactor :as transactor]\\n    18\\t            [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\\n    19\\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\\n    20\\t            [yin.vm.linker.authority :as authority]))\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t;; =============================================================================\\n    24\\t;; Fixtures: an in-memory dao.space, the A1/A2 signature stand-in, and\\n    25\\t;; the two reads a composition performs at a snapshot\\n    26\\t;; =============================================================================\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t(defn- addr\\n    29\\t  \\\"A distinct manifest address for a distinct payload.\\\"\\n    30\\t  [payload]\\n    31\\t  (jing/segment-key payload))\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t\\n    34\\t(defn- fake-sign\\n    35\\t  \\\"The 'signature' over an envelope: the blake3 digest of its canonical\\n    36\\t   bytes, as a plain hex string (the A1/A2 stand-in, unchanged).\\\"\\n    37\\t  [env]\\n    38\\t  (jing/content-hash env))\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\t(defn- fake-verify\\n    42\\t  [_key bs sig]\\n    43\\t  (= sig (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 bs)))\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\t\\n    46\\t(defn- sig-decl\\n    47\\t  [principal]\\n    48\\t  {:proof :yin.module/signature\\n    49\\t   :key [:key principal]\\n    50\\t   :verify fake-verify\\n    51\\t   :seq-floor 0})\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t\\n    54\\t(defn- attested-decl\\n    55\\t  [log-id]\\n    56\\t  {:proof :yin.module/attested :dao.stream/identity log-id})\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t(defn- assertion-env\\n    60\\t  [principal name-sym manifest n]\\n    61\\t  {:yin.module/op :assert\\n    62\\t   :yin.module/name name-sym\\n    63\\t   :yin.module/manifest manifest\\n    64\\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\\n    65\\t   :yin.module/seq n})\\n    66\\t\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t(defn- retraction-env\\n    69\\t  [principal asserted n]\\n    70\\t  {:yin.module/op :retract\\n    71\\t   :yin.module/of (authority/assertion-id asserted)\\n    72\\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\\n    73\\t   :yin.module/seq n})\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\t\\n    76\\t(defn- open-space\\n    77\\t  \\\"An in-memory dao.space: a transactor value over a complete-retention\\n    78\\t   memory-log local stream and a ringbuffer intake pool.\\\"\\n    79\\t  []\\n    80\\t  (let [mem (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log})\\n    81\\t        pool (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\\n    82\\t                                  :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity 64})]\\n    83\\t    (transactor/create!\\n    84\\t      {:local-stream (:dao.stream/handle mem)\\n    85\\t       :intake-pool [(:dao.stream/handle pool)]})))\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t(defn- commit!\\n    89\\t  \\\"Resolve tx-data against the retained history and commit it as one\\n    90\\t   atomic transaction. Answers the receipt, whose :dao.space/t is the\\n    91\\t   committed cursor position -- the snapshot the reads below bound to.\\\"\\n    92\\t  [log tx-data]\\n    93\\t  (let [prepared (transact/prepare-tx\\n    94\\t                   {:base-datoms (index/snapshot-datoms (:local-stream log))\\n    95\\t                    :tx-data tx-data})]\\n    96\\t    (transactor/transact! log (mapv #(assoc % 3 nil) (:datoms prepared)))))\\n    97\\t\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t(defn- signed-event\\n   100\\t  \\\"The section 8.2 datoms for one signed event: envelope and proof on\\n   101\\t   one event entity, `ev` a tempid.\\\"\\n   102\\t  [ev env]\\n   103\\t  [[:db/add ev :yin.module/envelope env]\\n   104\\t   [:db/add ev :yin.module/proof {:yin.module/signature (fake-sign env)}]])\\n   105\\t\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t(defn- events-at\\n   108\\t  \\\"The authority events visible at cursor position `t`: the retained\\n   109\\t   history under the `current` view, as-of bounded, its current facts\\n   110\\t   read through `match` and handed to ingestion. `carrier` is the\\n   111\\t   :dao.stream/identity of the stream this read is from, nil when the\\n   112\\t   read names none.\\\"\\n   113\\t  ([log t] (events-at log t nil))\\n   114\\t  ([log t carrier]\\n   115\\t   (let [view (query/current\\n   116\\t                (query/relation\\n   117\\t                  (index/snapshot-datoms (:local-stream log)))\\n   118\\t                t)]\\n   119\\t     (authority/events-from-datoms\\n   120\\t       (query/match view ['_ '_ '_])\\n   121\\t       carrier))))\\n   122\\t\\n   123\\t\\n   124\\t(defn- entry\\n   125\\t  [snapshot name-sym]\\n   126\\t  (get (:names snapshot) name-sym))\\n   127\\t\\n   128\\t\\n   129\\t(defn- discards\\n   130\\t  [snapshot kind]\\n   131\\t  (filter (fn [d] (= kind (:kind d))) (:diagnostics snapshot)))\\n   132\\t\\n   133\\t\\n   134\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   135\\t;; End to end from transacted datoms\\n   136\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   137\\t\\n   138\\t(deftest transacted-assertion-datoms-resolve-the-name\\n   139\\t  (let [log (open-space)\\n   140\\t        a (addr [:manifest 'my.lib 1])\\n   141\\t        receipt (commit! log (signed-event\\n   142\\t                               \\\"tid_ev\\\" (assertion-env 'alice 'my.lib a 1)))\\n   143\\t        t (:dao.space/t receipt)\\n   144\\t        snap (authority/name-environment\\n   145\\t               {:snapshot t :principals {'alice (sig-decl 'alice)}}\\n   146\\t               (events-at log t))]\\n   147\\t    ;; the first committed transaction is cursor position 0\\n   148\\t    (is (= 0 t))\\n   149\\t    (is (= {'my.lib {:status :ok\\n   150\\t                     :address a\\n   151\\t                     :yin.link/provenance\\n   152\\t                     {:yin.module/asserted-by ['alice]\\n   153\\t                      :yin.link/proof-kind [:yin.module/signature]\\n   154\\t                      :yin.link/snapshot 0}}}\\n   155\\t           (:names snap)))\\n   156\\t    (is (empty? (:diagnostics snap)))\\n   157\\t    (is (= {'alice 1} (:honored-seq snap)))))\\n   158\\t\\n   159\\t\\n   160\\t(deftest datom-transacted-after-the-snapshot-is-invisible-until-rebuilt\\n   161\\t  (let [log (open-space)\\n   162\\t        old (addr [:m 'my.lib 1])\\n   163\\t        new (addr [:m 'your.lib 2])\\n   164\\t        t1 (:dao.space/t\\n   165\\t             (commit! log (signed-event\\n   166\\t                            \\\"tid_1\\\" (assertion-env 'alice 'my.lib old 1))))\\n   167\\t        ;; transacted after the first snapshot's cursor position; the\\n   168\\t        ;; reads below happen after both commits, so the bound alone\\n   169\\t        ;; decides what each snapshot sees\\n   170\\t        t2 (:dao.space/t\\n   171\\t             (commit! log (signed-event\\n   172\\t                            \\\"tid_2\\\" (assertion-env 'alice 'your.lib new 2))))\\n   173\\t        snap1 (authority/name-environment\\n   174\\t                {:snapshot t1 :principals {'alice (sig-decl 'alice)}}\\n   175\\t                (events-at log t1))\\n   176\\t        ;; the composition advances: a fresh read at the new cursor\\n   177\\t        snap2 (authority/name-environment\\n   178\\t                {:snapshot t2 :principals {'alice (sig-decl 'alice)}}\\n   179\\t                (events-at log t2))]\\n   180\\t    (is (= :ok (:status (entry snap1 'my.lib))))\\n   181\\t    (is (= old (:address (entry snap1 'my.lib))))\\n   182\\t    ;; invisible at the first snapshot: no name, no event, no diagnostic\\n   183\\t    (is (nil? (entry snap1 'your.lib)))\\n   184\\t    (is (empty? (:diagnostics snap1)))\\n   185\\t    ;; the first snapshot is a value: the second build changed nothing of it\\n   186\\t    (is (= {'my.lib {:status :ok\\n   187\\t                     :address old\\n   188\\t                     :yin.link/provenance\\n   189\\t                     {:yin.module/asserted-by ['alice]\\n   190\\t                      :yin.link/proof-kind [:yin.module/signature]\\n   191\\t                      :yin.link/snapshot t1}}}\\n   192\\t           (:names snap1)))\\n   193\\t    ;; at the rebuilt snapshot the later datom exists\\n   194\\t    (is (= :ok (:status (entry snap2 'your.lib))))\\n   195\\t    (is (= new (:address (entry snap2 'your.lib))))\\n   196\\t    (is (= t2 (-> (entry snap2 'your.lib)\\n   197\\t                  :yin.link/provenance :yin.link/snapshot)))\\n   198\\t    (is (= {'alice 2} (:honored-seq snap2)))))\\n   199\\t\\n   200\\t\\n   201\\t(deftest transacted-retraction-removes-exactly-its-assertion\\n   202\\t  (let [log (open-space)\\n   203\\t        doomed-env (assertion-env 'alice 'my.lib (addr [:m 'my.lib 1]) 1)\\n   204\\t        kept (addr [:m 'my.lib 3])\\n   205\\t        other (addr [:m 'other.lib 2])\\n   206\\t        tx-data (concat\\n   207\\t                  (signed-event \\\"tid_1\\\" doomed-env)\\n   208\\t                  (signed-event \\\"tid_2\\\"\\n   209\\t                                (assertion-env 'alice 'my.lib kept 2))\\n   210\\t                  (signed-event \\\"tid_3\\\"\\n   211\\t                                (assertion-env 'alice 'other.lib other 3))\\n   212\\t                  (signed-event \\\"tid_4\\\" (retraction-env 'alice doomed-env 4)))\\n   213\\t        t (:dao.space/t (commit! log tx-data))\\n   214\\t        snap (authority/name-environment\\n   215\\t               {:snapshot t :principals {'alice (sig-decl 'alice)}}\\n   216\\t               (events-at log t))]\\n   217\\t    ;; the retracted id is gone; the same-named sibling survives it\\n   218\\t    (is (= :ok (:status (entry snap 'my.lib))))\\n   219\\t    (is (= kept (:address (entry snap 'my.lib))))\\n   220\\t    (is (= other (:address (entry snap 'other.lib))))\\n   221\\t    (is (empty? (discards snap :dangling-retraction)))\\n   222\\t    (is (= {'alice 4} (:honored-seq snap)))))\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\t\\n   225\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   226\\t;; Malformed datoms fail closed through the policy\\n   227\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   228\\t\\n   229\\t(deftest malformed-authority-datoms-fail-closed\\n   230\\t  (let [log (open-space)\\n   231\\t        env (assertion-env 'alice 'my.lib (addr [:m 1]) 1)\\n   232\\t        t (:dao.space/t\\n   233\\t            (commit! log\\n   234\\t                     [;; an envelope datom with no proof datom\\n   235\\t                      [:db/add \\\"tid_1\\\" :yin.module/envelope env]\\n   236\\t                      ;; a proof datom with no envelope datom\\n   237\\t                      [:db/add \\\"tid_2\\\" :yin.module/proof\\n   238\\t                       {:yin.module/signature (fake-sign env)}]\\n   239\\t                      ;; an envelope datom whose value is no envelope\\n   240\\t                      [:db/add \\\"tid_3\\\" :yin.module/envelope\\n   241\\t                       \\\"not an envelope\\\"]]))\\n   242\\t        events (events-at log t)\\n   243\\t        snap (authority/name-environment\\n   244\\t               {:snapshot t :principals {'alice (sig-decl 'alice)}}\\n   245\\t               events)]\\n   246\\t    ;; one event per envelope datom; the orphan proof names no event\\n   247\\t    (is (= 2 (count events)))\\n   248\\t    (is (= :absent (:reason (entry snap 'my.lib))))\\n   249\\t    ;; only the no-proof and the malformed-envelope kinds appear\\n   250\\t    (is (= #{:no-proof :malformed-envelope}\\n   251\\t           (set (map :kind (:diagnostics snap)))))\\n   252\\t    (is (= 1 (count (discards snap :no-proof))))\\n   253\\t    (is (= 1 (count (discards snap :malformed-envelope))))\\n   254\\t    (is (= :not-an-envelope\\n   255\\t           (:defect (first (discards snap :malformed-envelope)))))))\\n   256\\t\\n   257\\t\\n   258\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   259\\t;; The carrier of the read gates attested proofs\\n   260\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   261\\t\\n   262\\t(deftest attested-datoms-prove-only-through-the-reads-carrier\\n   263\\t  (let [log (open-space)\\n   264\\t        a (addr [:m 1])\\n   265\\t        env (assertion-env 'reporter 'log.lib a 1)\\n   266\\t        t (:dao.space/t\\n   267\\t            (commit! log\\n   268\\t                     [[:db/add \\\"tid_ev\\\" :yin.module/envelope env]\\n   269\\t                      [:db/add \\\"tid_ev\\\" :yin.module/proof\\n   270\\t                       {:yin.module/attested :dao.stream/log-1}]]))\\n   271\\t        decls {'reporter (attested-decl :dao.stream/log-1)}]\\n   272\\t    (testing \\\"read from the declared stream, the envelope is proven\\\"\\n   273\\t      (let [snap (authority/name-environment\\n   274\\t                   {:snapshot t :principals decls}\\n   275\\t                   (events-at log t :dao.stream/log-1))]\\n   276\\t        (is (= :ok (:status (entry snap 'log.lib))))\\n   277\\t        (is (= a (:address (entry snap 'log.lib))))\\n   278\\t        (is (empty? (:diagnostics snap)))))\\n   279\\t    (testing \\\"the same datoms read from nowhere carry no proof\\\"\\n   280\\t      (let [snap (authority/name-environment\\n   281\\t                   {:snapshot t :principals decls}\\n   282\\t                   (events-at log t))]\\n   283\\t        (is (= :absent (:reason (entry snap 'log.lib))))\\n   284\\t        (is (= 1 (count (discards snap :bad-proof))))))))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc | sed -n '1,500p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t(ns yin.vm.linker.authority\\n     2\\t  \\\"Section 8.2 of docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md: the fail-closed,\\n     3\\t   proof-carrying name-authority policy behind the linker's name\\n     4\\t   environment. `name-environment` is a pure function over plain data:\\n     5\\t   it folds an authority map and a sequence of authority events\\n     6\\t   (assertion and retraction envelopes with their proofs) into a\\n     7\\t   name-environment snapshot plus diagnostics, and touches no stream,\\n     8\\t   no format record, no fetch path, and no kernel. The only\\n     9\\t   dependencies are the committed `dao.jing` content identities\\n    10\\t   (`segment-key`, `canonical-bytes`) and the composition-supplied\\n    11\\t   verify function the authority map carries: no cryptographic\\n    12\\t   primitive is implemented here.\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t  Envelope shapes, the three per-principal passes, the retraction\\n    15\\t  binding, and the per-name fold are exactly the section 8.2 policy:\\n    16\\t  shape-validated envelopes by declared principals are honored only\\n    17\\t  with a valid proof; duplicates collapse by content id; equal\\n    18\\t  sequences from one principal are equivocation; sequences at or below\\n    19\\t  the floor are replays; a retraction removes exactly the assertion\\n    20\\t  its :yin.module/of names; and more than one remaining manifest\\n    21\\t  address for a name refuses :ambiguous-name with no tie-break rule.\\\"\\n    22\\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]))\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t;; =============================================================================\\n    26\\t;; Envelopes and content ids (section 8.2)\\n    27\\t;; =============================================================================\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t(defn assertion-id\\n    30\\t  \\\"The content address of an authority envelope: its `dao.jing`\\n    31\\t   segment-key. This is the id a retraction's :yin.module/of names.\\\"\\n    32\\t  [env]\\n    33\\t  (jing/segment-key env))\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\t(defn- envelope-defect\\n    37\\t  \\\"The first shape defect of env, or nil when env is a well-formed\\n    38\\t   assertion or retraction envelope. Manifest and retraction target\\n    39\\t   are checked by `dao.jing/segment-address?`, the authoritative\\n    40\\t   closed-registry address check.\\\"\\n    41\\t  [env]\\n    42\\t  (if (map? env)\\n    43\\t    (case (get env :yin.module/op)\\n    44\\t      :assert (cond\\n    45\\t                (not (symbol? (get env :yin.module/name))) :bad-name\\n    46\\t                (not (jing/segment-address?\\n    47\\t                       (get env :yin.module/manifest))) :bad-manifest\\n    48\\t                (nil? (get env :yin.module/asserted-by)) :bad-asserted-by\\n    49\\t                :else (if (int? (get env :yin.module/seq)) nil :bad-seq))\\n    50\\t      :retract (cond\\n    51\\t                 (not (jing/segment-address?\\n    52\\t                        (get env :yin.module/of))) :bad-of\\n    53\\t                 (nil? (get env :yin.module/asserted-by)) :bad-asserted-by\\n    54\\t                 :else (if (int? (get env :yin.module/seq)) nil :bad-seq))\\n    55\\t      :bad-op)\\n    56\\t    :not-an-envelope))\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t;; =============================================================================\\n    60\\t;; Datom ingestion (section 8.2)\\n    61\\t;; =============================================================================\\n    62\\t\\n    63\\t(defn events-from-datoms\\n    64\\t  \\\"The section 8.2 authority event sequence, assembled from the\\n    65\\t   assertion datoms a composition read at its snapshot: every\\n    66\\t   `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]` datom yields one event whose proof is\\n    67\\t   the first `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]` datom of the same entity.\\n    68\\t   An envelope datom with no proof datom is the no-proof case the policy\\n    69\\t   discards as :unauthenticated; a proof datom with no envelope datom\\n    70\\t   names no event and is ignored -- section 8.2's diagnostic kinds are a\\n    71\\t   closed set, and an orphan proof is no envelope at all. `carrier` is\\n    72\\t   the :dao.stream/identity of the one stream the composition read at\\n    73\\t   the snapshot, marked on every event for the attested check; nil means\\n    74\\t   the read names no stream, and an attested proof fails :bad-proof\\n    75\\t   there. Events keep the handed datoms' order, and the datoms are\\n    76\\t   already snapshot-bounded by the reader: nothing here reads or\\n    77\\t   advances a snapshot itself.\\\"\\n    78\\t  ([datoms] (events-from-datoms datoms nil))\\n    79\\t  ([datoms carrier]\\n    80\\t   (let [proof-of (reduce (fn [acc [e a v]]\\n    81\\t                            (if (and (= a :yin.module/proof)\\n    82\\t                                     (not (contains? acc e)))\\n    83\\t                              (assoc acc e v)\\n    84\\t                              acc))\\n    85\\t                          {}\\n    86\\t                          datoms)]\\n    87\\t     (into []\\n    88\\t           (keep (fn [[e a v]]\\n    89\\t                   (when (= a :yin.module/envelope)\\n    90\\t                     (cond-> {:yin.module/envelope v}\\n    91\\t                       (contains? proof-of e)\\n    92\\t                       (assoc :yin.module/proof (get proof-of e))\\n    93\\t                       (some? carrier)\\n    94\\t                       (assoc :dao.stream/identity carrier)))))\\n    95\\t           datoms))))\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\t\\n    98\\t;; =============================================================================\\n    99\\t;; Authentication: the two proof kinds (section 8.2)\\n   100\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   101\\t\\n   102\\t(defn- proof-state\\n   103\\t  \\\"nil when the event's proof is valid for the principal's declaration,\\n   104\\t   else the authentication failure: :no-proof, :bad-proof, or\\n   105\\t   :no-proof-kind when the declaration admits neither proof kind and\\n   106\\t   the principal cannot assert anything. The verify function's answer\\n   107\\t   is taken as given; it is composition-supplied host code and is\\n   108\\t   expected not to throw.\\\"\\n   109\\t  [decl event]\\n   110\\t  (let [proof (get event :yin.module/proof)]\\n   111\\t    (case (get decl :proof)\\n   112\\t      :yin.module/signature\\n   113\\t      (if (map? proof)\\n   114\\t        (let [sig (get proof :yin.module/signature)]\\n   115\\t          (if (nil? sig)\\n   116\\t            :no-proof\\n   117\\t            (let [verify (get decl :verify)]\\n   118\\t              (when-not (and verify\\n   119\\t                             (verify (get decl :key)\\n   120\\t                                     (jing/canonical-bytes\\n   121\\t                                       (get event :yin.module/envelope))\\n   122\\t                                     sig))\\n   123\\t                :bad-proof))))\\n   124\\t        :no-proof)\\n   125\\t      :yin.module/attested\\n   126\\t      (if (map? proof)\\n   127\\t        (let [declared (get decl :dao.stream/identity)]\\n   128\\t          (if (nil? (get proof :yin.module/attested))\\n   129\\t            :no-proof\\n   130\\t            ;; the envelope must have been read from the declared log:\\n   131\\t            ;; copied onto another stream it carries no proof\\n   132\\t            (if (or (not= declared (get proof :yin.module/attested))\\n   133\\t                    (not= declared (get event :dao.stream/identity)))\\n   134\\t              :bad-proof\\n   135\\t              nil)))\\n   136\\t        :no-proof)\\n   137\\t      :no-proof-kind)))\\n   138\\t\\n   139\\t\\n   140\\t(defn- discard-reason\\n   141\\t  \\\"The section 8.2 discard reason of an authentication failure kind.\\\"\\n   142\\t  [kind]\\n   143\\t  (case kind\\n   144\\t    :no-proof :unauthenticated\\n   145\\t    :bad-proof :unauthenticated\\n   146\\t    :no-proof-kind :undeclared-principal\\n   147\\t    kind))\\n   148\\t\\n   149\\t\\n   150\\t(defn- env-diagnostic\\n   151\\t  \\\"The diagnostic entry for one discarded envelope.\\\"\\n   152\\t  [kind reason env extra]\\n   153\\t  (merge {:kind kind\\n   154\\t          :reason reason\\n   155\\t          :id (when (some? env) (assertion-id env))\\n   156\\t          :op (when (map? env) (get env :yin.module/op))\\n   157\\t          :principal (when (map? env) (get env :yin.module/asserted-by))\\n   158\\t          :seq (when (map? env) (get env :yin.module/seq))}\\n   159\\t         extra))\\n   160\\t\\n   161\\t\\n   162\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   163\\t;; The three per-principal passes (section 8.2)\\n   164\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   165\\t\\n   166\\t(defn- honor-passes\\n   167\\t  \\\"The three passes over one principal's proven envelopes: deduplicate\\n   168\\t   by content id (duplicate appearances beyond the first drop\\n   169\\t   silently), detect equivocation on equal sequence (every envelope of\\n   170\\t   the principal from the first equivocating sequence on is discarded\\n   171\\t   as equivocation), then order by sequence and honor each envelope\\n   172\\t   only past the floor and every sequence honored before it. Returns\\n   173\\t   {:honored [...] :diagnostics [...]}.\\\"\\n   174\\t  [decl proven]\\n   175\\t  (let [deduped (::kept\\n   176\\t                  (reduce (fn [acc cand]\\n   177\\t                            (if (contains? (::seen acc) (:id cand))\\n   178\\t                              acc\\n   179\\t                              (-> acc\\n   180\\t                                  (update ::kept conj cand)\\n   181\\t                                  (update ::seen conj (:id cand)))))\\n   182\\t                          {::kept [] ::seen #{}}\\n   183\\t                          proven))\\n   184\\t        by-seq (group-by :seq deduped)\\n   185\\t        eq-min (when-let [eqs (seq (keep (fn [[s cands]]\\n   186\\t                                           (when (> (count cands) 1) s))\\n   187\\t                                         by-seq))]\\n   188\\t                 (reduce min eqs))\\n   189\\t        {kept :kept equated :equated}\\n   190\\t        (if eq-min\\n   191\\t          (group-by (fn [cand]\\n   192\\t                      (if (>= (:seq cand) eq-min)\\n   193\\t                        :equated :kept))\\n   194\\t                    deduped)\\n   195\\t          {:kept deduped})\\n   196\\t        floor (or (get decl :seq-floor) 0)\\n   197\\t        done (reduce (fn [acc cand]\\n   198\\t                       (if (> (:seq cand) (::last-honored acc))\\n   199\\t                         (-> acc\\n   200\\t                             (assoc ::last-honored (:seq cand))\\n   201\\t                             (update ::honored conj cand))\\n   202\\t                         (update acc ::replayed conj cand)))\\n   203\\t                     {::last-honored floor ::honored [] ::replayed []}\\n   204\\t                     (sort-by :seq (or kept [])))]\\n   205\\t    {:honored (::honored done)\\n   206\\t     :diagnostics\\n   207\\t     (into (mapv (fn [cand]\\n   208\\t                   (env-diagnostic :equivocation :equivocation\\n   209\\t                                   (:env cand) nil))\\n   210\\t                 (or equated []))\\n   211\\t           (mapv (fn [cand]\\n   212\\t                   (env-diagnostic :replay :replay (:env cand) nil))\\n   213\\t                 (::replayed done)))}))\\n   214\\t\\n   215\\t\\n   216\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   217\\t;; The per-name fold (section 8.2)\\n   218\\t;; =============================================================================\\n   219\\t\\n   220\\t(defn- name-entry\\n   221\\t  \\\"The outcome for one name: :absent for zero remaining assertions, a\\n   222\\t   successful resolution with provenance for exactly one distinct\\n   223\\t   manifest address, :ambiguous-name naming every remaining address\\n   224\\t   and asserter for more than one. Entries are ordered by address, so\\n   225\\t   the outcome never depends on carrier order, recency, or sequence.\\\"\\n   226\\t  [decls snapshot cands]\\n   227\\t  (let [entries (sort-by (fn [e] (str (:address e) \\\" \\\" (:asserter e)))\\n   228\\t                         (distinct\\n   229\\t                           (map (fn [cand]\\n   230\\t                                  {:address (get (:env cand)\\n   231\\t                                                 :yin.module/manifest)\\n   232\\t                                   :asserter (:principal cand)})\\n   233\\t                                cands)))\\n   234\\t        addresses (distinct (map :address entries))\\n   235\\t        asserters (distinct (map :asserter entries))]\\n   236\\t    (case (count addresses)\\n   237\\t      0 {:status :refused :reason :absent}\\n   238\\t      1 {:status :ok\\n   239\\t         :address (first addresses)\\n   240\\t         :yin.link/provenance\\n   241\\t         {:yin.module/asserted-by (vec asserters)\\n   242\\t          :yin.link/proof-kind\\n   243\\t          (vec (distinct (map (fn [p] (get (get decls p) :proof))\\n   244\\t                              asserters)))\\n   245\\t          :yin.link/snapshot snapshot}}\\n   246\\t      {:status :refused\\n   247\\t       :reason :ambiguous-name\\n   248\\t       :addresses (vec addresses)\\n   249\\t       :asserters (vec asserters)})))\\n   250\\t\\n   251\\t\\n   252\\t(defn name-environment\\n   253\\t  \\\"Fold `events` under `authority` into the name-environment snapshot\\n   254\\t   of section 8.2.\\n   255\\t\\n   256\\t   `authority` is a map with the snapshot under :snapshot (an index\\n   257\\t   manifest address or a stream cursor; it is echoed and never\\n   258\\t   dereferenced here) and the accepted principals under :principals.\\n   259\\t   A signature principal declares {:proof :yin.module/signature\\n   260\\t   :key k :verify f}; f is composition-supplied and is called as\\n   261\\t   (f key canonical-bytes sig). An attested principal declares\\n   262\\t   {:proof :yin.module/attested :dao.stream/identity id} and every\\n   263\\t   envelope must have been read from that stream. Either may carry\\n   264\\t   :seq-floor, the highest sequence already honored for a re-declared\\n   265\\t   principal (0 for a new one).\\n   266\\t\\n   267\\t   Each event is a map: :yin.module/envelope, :yin.module/proof, and,\\n   268\\t   for the attested check, the :dao.stream/identity the envelope was\\n   269\\t   read from. An envelope whose proof is absent or fails is\\n   270\\t   :unauthenticated and is discarded before counting.\\n   271\\t\\n   272\\t   Returns {:names {name entry} :diagnostics [...] :honored-seq\\n   273\\t   {principal highest-honored-sequence} :snapshot s}. Advancing the\\n   274\\t   snapshot is a fresh call with the advanced authority and events\\n   275\\t   (the next floor is :honored-seq), never an ambient re-read.\\\"\\n   276\\t  [authority events]\\n   277\\t  (let [decls (:principals authority)\\n   278\\t        {stage1 :diagnostics proven :proven name-set :names}\\n   279\\t        (reduce\\n   280\\t          (fn [acc event]\\n   281\\t            (let [env (when (map? event)\\n   282\\t                        (get event :yin.module/envelope))]\\n   283\\t              (if-some [defect (envelope-defect env)]\\n   284\\t                (update acc :diagnostics conj\\n   285\\t                        (env-diagnostic :malformed-envelope\\n   286\\t                                        :malformed-envelope\\n   287\\t                                        env {:defect defect}))\\n   288\\t                (let [principal (get env :yin.module/asserted-by)\\n   289\\t                      acc (if (= :assert (get env :yin.module/op))\\n   290\\t                            (update acc :names conj\\n   291\\t                                    (get env :yin.module/name))\\n   292\\t                            acc)]\\n   293\\t                  (if-not (contains? decls principal)\\n   294\\t                    (update acc :diagnostics conj\\n   295\\t                            (env-diagnostic :undeclared-principal\\n   296\\t                                            :undeclared-principal\\n   297\\t                                            env nil))\\n   298\\t                    (if-some [failed (proof-state (get decls principal)\\n   299\\t                                                  event)]\\n   300\\t                      (update acc :diagnostics conj\\n   301\\t                              (env-diagnostic failed\\n   302\\t                                              (discard-reason failed)\\n   303\\t                                              env nil))\\n   304\\t                      (update acc :proven conj\\n   305\\t                              {:env env\\n   306\\t                               :id (assertion-id env)\\n   307\\t                               :principal principal\\n   308\\t                               :seq (get env :yin.module/seq)})))))))\\n   309\\t          {:diagnostics [] :proven [] :names #{}}\\n   310\\t          events)\\n   311\\t        per-principal\\n   312\\t        (mapv (fn [principal]\\n   313\\t                (let [mine (filter (fn [cand]\\n   314\\t                                     (= principal (:principal cand)))\\n   315\\t                                   proven)\\n   316\\t                      {:keys [honored diagnostics]}\\n   317\\t                      (honor-passes (get decls principal) mine)]\\n   318\\t                  {:principal principal\\n   319\\t                   :honored honored\\n   320\\t                   :diagnostics diagnostics}))\\n   321\\t              (distinct (mapv :principal proven)))\\n   322\\t        honored (mapcat :honored per-principal)\\n   323\\t        {assertions true retractions false}\\n   324\\t        (group-by (fn [cand]\\n   325\\t                    (= :assert (get (:env cand) :yin.module/op)))\\n   326\\t                  honored)\\n   327\\t        by-principal (group-by :principal assertions)\\n   328\\t        {retracted true dangling false}\\n   329\\t        (group-by (fn [cand]\\n   330\\t                    (contains?\\n   331\\t                      (set (map :id (get by-principal\\n   332\\t                                         (:principal cand))))\\n   333\\t                      (get (:env cand) :yin.module/of)))\\n   334\\t                  (or retractions []))\\n   335\\t        retracted-ids (set (map (fn [cand]\\n   336\\t                                  (get (:env cand) :yin.module/of))\\n   337\\t                                (or retracted [])))\\n   338\\t        surviving (remove (fn [cand]\\n   339\\t                            (contains? retracted-ids (:id cand)))\\n   340\\t                          (or assertions []))\\n   341\\t        by-name (group-by (fn [cand]\\n   342\\t                            (get (:env cand) :yin.module/name))\\n   343\\t                          surviving)]\\n   344\\t    {:names (into {}\\n   345\\t                  (map (fn [nm]\\n   346\\t                         [nm (name-entry decls (:snapshot authority)\\n   347\\t                                         (get by-name nm))]))\\n   348\\t                  name-set)\\n   349\\t     :diagnostics (vec (concat stage1\\n   350\\t                               (mapcat :diagnostics per-principal)\\n   351\\t                               (map (fn [cand]\\n   352\\t                                      (env-diagnostic\\n   353\\t                                        :dangling-retraction\\n   354\\t                                        :dangling-retraction\\n   355\\t                                        (:env cand)\\n   356\\t                                        {:of (get (:env cand)\\n   357\\t                                                  :yin.module/of)}))\\n   358\\t                                    (or dangling []))))\\n   359\\t     :honored-seq (into {}\\n   360\\t                        (keep (fn [pr]\\n   361\\t                                (when (seq (:honored pr))\\n   362\\t                                  [(:principal pr)\\n   363\\t                                   (reduce max (map :seq (:honored pr)))])))\\n   364\\t                        per-principal)\\n   365\\t     :snapshot (:snapshot authority)}))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1680,1840p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '1680,1840p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"  1680\\t- The manifest is verified like any content: a `:yin.module/manifest`\\n  1681\\t  format record with `:identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?`, a\\n  1682\\t  validator over the keys above, no parts, no obligations.\\n  1683\\t\\n  1684\\t### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\\n  1685\\t\\n  1686\\tNames live outside the manifest. A name environment maps a module name\\n  1687\\tto a manifest address and is linker-local state in one of two shapes:\\n  1688\\t\\n  1689\\t- a plain map `{'my.lib :segment/...}`, for tests and single-process\\n  1690\\t  compositions, with the composition itself as the sole asserter;\\n  1691\\t- assertions read from a `dao.space` source under the policy below.\\n  1692\\t\\n  1693\\t**Fail-closed assertion policy.** This policy is an entry criterion for\\n  1694\\tM4: no linker may resolve a name from `dao.space` assertions before it is\\n  1695\\timplemented and tested. The policy lives in `yin.vm.linker.authority`,\\n  1696\\tas a pure function over plain data.\\n  1697\\t\\n  1698\\t- **Every authority event is a signed envelope.** An assertion and a\\n  1699\\t  retraction are two distinct envelope shapes, each a plain map whose\\n  1700\\t  content address (`dao.jing/segment-key`) is the event's id:\\n  1701\\t\\n  1702\\t  ```clojure\\n  1703\\t  ;; assertion\\n  1704\\t  {:yin.module/op          :assert\\n  1705\\t   :yin.module/name        'my.lib\\n  1706\\t   :yin.module/manifest    :segment/...\\n  1707\\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\\n  1708\\t   :yin.module/seq         41}          ; per-principal, strictly rising\\n  1709\\t\\n  1710\\t  ;; retraction: bound to one assertion by that assertion's id\\n  1711\\t  {:yin.module/op          :retract\\n  1712\\t   :yin.module/of          :segment/... ; segment-key of the assertion\\n  1713\\t   :yin.module/asserted-by principal\\n  1714\\t   :yin.module/seq         42}\\n  1715\\t  ```\\n  1716\\t\\n  1717\\t  The envelope is transacted as datoms `[ev :yin.module/envelope env]`\\n  1718\\t  and `[ev :yin.module/proof proof]`. Ingestion is\\n  1719\\t  `yin.vm.linker.authority/events-from-datoms`: one event per envelope\\n  1720\\t  datom, carrying its entity's first proof datom (an envelope with no\\n  1721\\t  proof datom is the no-proof case below; a proof datom with no envelope\\n  1722\\t  datom names no event and is ignored), with the carrier\\n  1723\\t  `:dao.stream/identity` of the read supplied by the composition, never\\n  1724\\t  read from a datom. An envelope is honored only with\\n  1725\\t  a proof; a bare `:asserted-by` value is a string anyone can write.\\n  1726\\t  An envelope whose proof is absent or fails is `:unauthenticated`\\n  1727\\t  with `:kind :no-proof` or `:bad-proof` and is discarded before\\n  1728\\t  counting. A retraction whose `:yin.module/of` names no assertion at\\n  1729\\t  the snapshot, or an assertion by a different principal, is discarded\\n  1730\\t  with `:kind :dangling-retraction`; a retraction retracts exactly the\\n  1731\\t  assertion it names and nothing by name alone.\\n  1732\\t- **Replay is prevented by the per-principal sequence.** Every envelope\\n  1733\\t  a principal issues carries `:yin.module/seq`, strictly increasing\\n  1734\\t  over that principal's lifetime; the composition declares each\\n  1735\\t  principal's floor in `:authority` (`0` for a new principal, the\\n  1736\\t  highest sequence already honored for a re-declared one). The\\n  1737\\t  declaration carries that floor as `:seq-floor`. At the snapshot the\\n  1738\\t  linker processes one principal's proven envelopes in three passes,\\n  1739\\t  in this order:\\n  1740\\t  1. *Deduplicate by content id.* Every envelope is content; two\\n  1741\\t     appearances of one envelope have one `segment-key` and are one\\n  1742\\t     event. All but the first appearance are dropped silently, as\\n  1743\\t     `dao.jing` drops a re-materialization: an exact duplicate is a\\n  1744\\t     harmless carrier replay (a forwarder, a retry after `full`, a\\n  1745\\t     mirrored log) and is neither a defect nor evidence against the\\n  1746\\t     principal. This pass runs first so that repeating a valid envelope\\n  1747\\t     can never suppress it.\\n  1748\\t  2. *Detect equivocation.* After deduplication, two *distinct*\\n  1749\\t     envelopes from one principal with equal sequence are equivocation:\\n  1750\\t     the principal signed two different claims under one sequence\\n  1751\\t     number. Both are discarded with `:kind :equivocation`, and the\\n  1752\\t     principal's later envelopes at the snapshot are discarded too. A\\n  1753\\t     duplicate can no longer reach this pass, so equivocation is\\n  1754\\t     attributable to the signer alone. The pair and every later\\n  1755\\t     envelope of that principal are discarded with\\n  1756\\t     `:kind :equivocation`.\\n  1757\\t  3. *Order and honor.* The remaining envelopes are ordered by sequence\\n  1758\\t     and each is honored only if its sequence exceeds the floor and\\n  1759\\t     every sequence honored before it; an envelope at or below either\\n  1760\\t     is a replay of an old claim under a fresh carrier and is discarded\\n  1761\\t     with `:kind :replay`.\\n  1762\\t  A monotone sequence is chosen over nonces because it makes the check\\n  1763\\t  stateless over the snapshot: no nonce store is needed and no window\\n  1764\\t  is guessed.\\n  1765\\t  A wall-clock timestamp is admitted as an optional\\n  1766\\t  `:yin.module/issued-at` in the envelope for audit, and is never used\\n  1767\\t  to order or to accept.\\n  1768\\t- Two proof kinds are admitted, and the composition's `:authority`\\n  1769\\t  declares, per principal, which one it expects:\\n  1770\\t  - *Signature.* `proof` is `{:yin.module/signature sig}`, where `sig`\\n  1771\\t    signs the canonical bytes (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) of the whole\\n  1772\\t    envelope under the principal's public key, so operation type, name,\\n  1773\\t    manifest, principal, and sequence are all covered and none can be\\n  1774\\t    altered or recombined. `:authority` holds, per principal, the key\\n  1775\\t    and a composition-supplied verify function; the linker calls the\\n  1776\\t    function and implements no cryptographic primitive itself (a host\\n  1777\\t    library sits behind the function, as `dao.jing` does for hashing).\\n  1778\\t    The signature is over content, so it survives every carrier and\\n  1779\\t    can be checked by any host that holds the key.\\n  1780\\t  - *Attested log.* The assertion stream is a one-writer log\\n  1781\\t    (`dao.stream.md`, *Concurrency*) whose writer the composition\\n  1782\\t    authenticated at attachment and bound to one principal; `:authority`\\n  1783\\t    names the stream's `:dao.stream/identity` beside that principal, and\\n  1784\\t    every envelope read from that identity, at the snapshot, counts as\\n  1785\\t    proven by it; `proof` is `{:yin.module/attested identity}` and the\\n  1786\\t    linker checks that the envelope was in fact read from that stream.\\n  1787\\t    The sequence rule applies unchanged, so a log that repeats an\\n  1788\\t    envelope repeats a replay. The proof holds only within the reach of\\n  1789\\t    the attachment discipline: an envelope copied off that log onto\\n  1790\\t    another medium carries no proof and is `:unauthenticated` there. A\\n  1791\\t    composition that needs envelopes to travel uses signatures.\\n  1792\\t  A principal declared with neither kind cannot assert anything.\\n  1793\\t- The linker's `:authority` names the accepted principals with their\\n  1794\\t  proof kind and material, and the **snapshot**: either a published\\n  1795\\t  index manifest address (`dao.space.index`) or a cursor position on\\n  1796\\t  the assertion stream. The linker reads exactly that snapshot;\\n  1797\\t  assertions appended afterwards do not exist for it until the\\n  1798\\t  composition advances the snapshot, which is an ordinary `link-state`\\n  1799\\t  rebuild, never an ambient re-read. The snapshot result carries\\n  1800\\t  `:honored-seq` per principal, the highest sequence honored in this\\n  1801\\t  snapshot, which the composition declares back as the next\\n  1802\\t  `:seq-floor`.\\n  1803\\t- At the snapshot, for one name: unauthenticated envelopes, exact\\n  1804\\t  duplicates beyond the first, replays, equivocations, and envelopes by\\n  1805\\t  undeclared principals are discarded or collapsed as the passes above\\n  1806\\t  say;\\n  1807\\t  each honored retraction removes exactly the assertion its\\n  1808\\t  `:yin.module/of` names; the distinct manifest addresses remaining are\\n  1809\\t  counted. Exactly one resolves the name. Zero is `:absent`. More than\\n  1810\\t  one is `:ambiguous-name` naming every remaining address and asserter,\\n  1811\\t  and no address is chosen by recency, sequence, order, or any other\\n  1812\\t  rule. Three shape and declaration diagnostics sit beside the four\\n  1813\\t  discard kinds: `:malformed-envelope` (an envelope that fails the\\n  1814\\t  shape gate), `:undeclared-principal` (an author the authority map\\n  1815\\t  does not declare), and `:no-proof-kind` (a principal declared with\\n  1816\\t  neither proof kind).\\n  1817\\t- Provenance is data the outcome carries: a successful resolution names\\n  1818\\t  the asserter, the proof kind, and the snapshot under\\n  1819\\t  `:yin.link/provenance` so a receiver can record which claim it acted\\n  1820\\t  on.\\n  1821\\t\\n  1822\\tAn entry is a claim. The manifest it names is verified, and its name is\\n  1823\\tverified against the entry (section 8.1). Which principals a composition\\n  1824\\tdeclares, and how it obtains and rotates their keys, is the composition's\\n  1825\\t(section 12); what the linker does with a declared principal's assertion\\n  1826\\tis fixed above.\\n  1827\\t\\n  1828\\t### 8.3 What `yin.vm.module` becomes\\n  1829\\t\\n  1830\\tThe namespace keeps its shape and changes its contents.\\n  1831\\t\\n  1832\\t| Today                        | After                                       |\\n  1833\\t|------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|\\n  1834\\t| `register-module r name fns` | `register-host-module r name fns profiles`  |\\n  1835\\t|                              | (rules below); no code fetched, because the |\\n  1836\\t|                              | host is the boundary                        |\\n  1837\\t| `resolve-module r sym`       | unchanged signature; reads the task-local   |\\n  1838\\t|                              | lowered `:bindings`                         |\\n  1839\\t| `require-handler`            | registry hit answers; installing joins the  |\\n  1840\\t|                              | waiter set; miss mints, parks, and emits    |\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \\\"events-from-datoms|index-from-datoms|yin.module/proof|yin.module/envelope|dao.stream/identity\\\" src/cljc/yin/vm test/yin/vm docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | head -220'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \\\"events-from-datoms|index-from-datoms|yin.module/proof|yin.module/envelope|dao.stream/identity\\\" src/cljc/yin/vm test/yin/vm docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | head -220'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:107: :yin.k/arbitration {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}     ; §7.7.3  the authority medium, named in the value\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:525: :yin.k/stream   {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}   ; the target\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:533: :yin.k/request    {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}   ; where the request went\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:534: :yin.k/response   {:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …}   ; where the answer lands\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:621:| stream reference | `:yin.k/stream` | `:dao.stream/identity … :dao.stream/descriptor …` | an attached handle, under a fresh store key |\\ntest/yin/vm/linker_authority_test.cljc:51:  {:proof :yin.module/attested :dao.stream/identi